      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general this change LGTM (we do not need to care about such legacy hardware) although I do not understand why we can\u0027t support hw requiring write buffer flash as `flush_write_buffer` that we have in arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c seems to handle that case correctly (at least at first glance): it write buffer flash command by setting DMA_GCMD_WBF.\n\nIf above is not enough (I see that `flush_write_buffer` is used in pKVM code in various places e.g. `pkvm_cache_tag_flush_range_np`, `pkvm_pasid_flush_caches` and `context_present_cache_flush`) and we really need to drop support for hw requiring WBF, maybe we should add TODO here to look closer to it in 6.18 and maybe clean-up the code and removing the illusion that we support it and also getting rid of dead pKVM code. WDYT?",
      "revId": "a07971f554b9bb482bb129c84f2357628d80818a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
